release: remove docs/verification references from public files; drop local path

- Remove all 32 references to docs/verification/** from the 16 public/shipped
  files, replacing each with a descriptive internal-record name that keeps the
  review ids, commit shas and run ids (for example "independent review R-010 at
  105fba5 (internal verification record, not published)"). README now points at
  docs/release-1.0.0.md instead of internal records.
- development-tools.lock.json: drop the /home/mitko/dev/casa/.venv path from the
  O1 source description and describe the owner-supplied interpreter without it.
- Shipped files (README.md, docs/release-1.0.0.md) no longer cite the private
  frozen revision 779e73f; verification is described without a private sha (the
  concrete binding will be re-issued against the public tip after curation). Run
  ids and artifact digests are retained.
- Deliberate extra edit beyond the citation rewrite: corrected two stale README
  claims that live local-model acceptance and the Pi requalification were
  unexecuted. Both passed (G8 run-58f5589ef776 and re-run run-85d1c3a117ef; Pi
  1.1.0 requalified, task-19). README is embedded in the wheel METADATA, so the
  wording had to be final before the artifact rebuild; flagged to the Lead.
- Verification: `git grep -n "docs/verification" -- . | grep -v '^docs/verification/'`
  is empty; development-tools.lock.json and BACKLOG.yaml parse; scripts/dev check
  exits 0 (74 files).
